+## D8 — Lesson-local conflict attributes remain underdetermined (review-94fce2532ffa954b)
+
+**Finding.** Version 2.2.0 varies the occupied-pair orbit globally but normally
+places only one unequal occupied pair in each three-demonstration window. A
+finite family of conditional rivals can therefore swap only adjacent or far
+pairs, border or interior pairs, one coordinate parity, or one color ordering.
+Across 4,608 generated windows (128 seeds × three bands × twelve starts), 1,437
+windows admitted at least one such query-changing rival. This does not invalidate
+the selected Racket rule; it exposes a lesson-local teaching ambiguity.
+
+**Retained witness.** For easy seed 70,000 at start 2, the demonstrations have
+a distance-four conflict followed by two no-conflict examples. The query has a
+distance-one conflict. `far_conflicts_only` fits all demonstrations and differs
+from the canonical query at two cells. Protected Racket evaluated all four
+inputs and matched the Python canonical mirror. Exact material is in
+`counterexamples/review-94fce2532ffa954b-v0001/`.
+
+**Decision.** Do not rush a production rewrite in this optional review. Retain
+`workspace/conflict_condition_probe.py`, make its source loading portable in the
+task tests, and leave version 2.2.0 unchanged. The next repair should
+constructively put at least two unequal conflicts with contrasting distance,
+border/interior position, color order, and parity inside every three-demo
+lesson while preserving lower/upper directional and immutable-snapshot
+evidence. Re-run the probe and protected-Racket labels after that change.
